From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Englund <tomenglund26@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 03:18:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia: make the coherent page fallback work for multi-page
 allocations

When a contiguous allocation fails on a vGPU host, nv_alloc_contig_pages()
falls back to nv_alloc_coherent_pages(), but at->order is already set, so
nv_compute_gfp_mask() adds __GFP_COMP. dma_alloc_attrs() warns and returns
NULL for that, so the fallback could never succeed for more than one page.
Without __GFP_COMP, dma-iommu could still return a remapped discontiguous
buffer, for which the virt_to_phys() page table setup would be wrong.

Drop __GFP_COMP and ask for a contiguous allocation.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 kernel-open/nvidia/nv-vm.c | 21 ++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-vm.c b/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-vm.c
index f1902973..811c4598 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-vm.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-vm.c
@@ -396,12 +396,18 @@ static NV_STATUS nv_alloc_coherent_pages(
     nvl = NV_GET_NVL_FROM_NV_STATE(nv);
     dev = nvl->dev;
 
-    gfp_mask = nv_compute_gfp_mask(nv, at);
+    /*
+     * The DMA API rejects __GFP_COMP, which at->order > 0 adds. The page table
+     * below needs linear addresses, so don't let dma-iommu use a remapped,
+     * discontiguous allocation.
+     */
+    gfp_mask = nv_compute_gfp_mask(nv, at) & ~__GFP_COMP;
 
-    virt_addr = (unsigned long)dma_alloc_coherent(dev,
-                                                  at->num_pages * PAGE_SIZE,
-                                                  &at->dma_handle,
-                                                  gfp_mask);
+    virt_addr = (unsigned long)dma_alloc_attrs(dev,
+                                               at->num_pages * PAGE_SIZE,
+                                               &at->dma_handle,
+                                               gfp_mask,
+                                               DMA_ATTR_FORCE_CONTIGUOUS);
     if (!virt_addr)
     {
         nv_printf(NV_DBG_MEMINFO,
@@ -440,8 +446,9 @@ static void nv_free_coherent_pages(
         nv_set_memory_type(at, 0, at->num_pages, NV_MEMORY_WRITEBACK);
     }
 
-    dma_free_coherent(dev, at->num_pages * PAGE_SIZE,
-                      (void *)page_ptr->virt_addr, at->dma_handle);
+    dma_free_attrs(dev, at->num_pages * PAGE_SIZE,
+                   (void *)page_ptr->virt_addr, at->dma_handle,
+                   DMA_ATTR_FORCE_CONTIGUOUS);
 }
 
 typedef struct
